  "notes": "Balance table for terrain_nomads. Every reach is a multiple of settlement spacing, never a metre constant, so a wider world does not turn a local band into a regional one. Speeds are absolute metres per day because a walking pace is a property of the traveller, not of the world. Gates are hard: a classification whose preconditions fail is ineligible outright, and a candidate that satisfies none produces no band at all. Thresholds are tuned so each hard gate admits a minority of land: most ground raises nobody, and a cult needs genuinely charged sacred ground rather than any ley whisper.",
